  "live_records": {
    "q-149701": {
      "dom_id": "step-q149701",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{3}{{x}^{4}},\\,x\\ge 1.\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe compute the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }3{x}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={-\\frac{3}{x}|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-\\frac{3}{1}) \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
