    "q-149702": {
      "dom_id": "step-q149702",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}, & 1<x\\le 2, \\\\ \\frac{x}{5}, & 2\\le x<3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{x}{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\,{|}_{1}^{2}+{\\frac{{x}^{4}}{20}|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =(2-1)+(\\frac{81}{20}-\\frac{16}{20}) \\\\  & =1+\\frac{13}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
