    "q-152898": {
      "dom_id": "step-q152898",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}, & 0<x<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}, & 1\\le x<3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\,{x}^{5}\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+x\\,{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(1-0)+(3-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
