    "q-152924": {
      "dom_id": "step-q152924",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}, & 0\\le x<1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\,x, & 1\\le x\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{4}].$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the fourth raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{4}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{4}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{4}\\cdot {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{7}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\,{x}^{8}\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{1}{12}\\,{x}^{6}\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}(1-0)+\\frac{1}{12}(64-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{21}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{43}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
