    "q-152920": {
      "dom_id": "step-q152920",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1-{x}^{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ \\frac{8}{9{x}^{3}}, & 1<x\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{3}].$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the third raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{3}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3}\\cdot (1-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{8}{9{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{3}-{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{8}{9}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{4}\\,{x}^{4}-\\frac{1}{6}\\,{x}^{6}){|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{8}{9}\\,x\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{6}-0)+\\frac{8}{9}(2-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}+\\frac{8}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{36}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
