    "q-131153": {
      "dom_id": "step-q131153",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[10-4{X}^{2}].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}},\\,1<x<2\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we simplify using the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[10-4{X}^{2}]=10-4\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the second raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=2$ into the simplified expression, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[10-4{X}^{2}] & =10-4\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] \\\\  & =10-4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
