    "q-90279": {
      "dom_id": "step-q90279",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[4{X}^{2}-3].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{x}{4},\\,1<x<3\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we simplify using the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[4{X}^{2}-3]=4\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-3\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the second raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{4}}{16}|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=5$ into the simplified expression, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[4{X}^{2}-3] & =4\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-3 \\\\  & =4\\cdot 5-3 \\\\  & =17.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
